1
00:00:00,360 --> 00:00:04,590
Teams often judge an agent migration from the final answer alone.

2
00:00:04,590 --> 00:00:09,205
That hides whether the workflow gained evidence, preserved constraints, or introduced contradictions.

3
00:00:09,205 --> 00:00:19,204
SOL Lens turns observable agent activity into an inspectable semantic comparison and asks a more useful question: did the candidate actually improve on the reference agent?

4
00:00:20,104 --> 00:00:28,331
Here, SOL means Self-Organizing Logos, the research framework behind this project - not the GPT-5.6 Sol model name.

5
00:00:28,331 --> 00:00:32,445
The SOL Engine is the mathematical and experimental foundation.

6
00:00:32,445 --> 00:00:38,844
SOL Lens is the browser workbench applying a smaller deterministic profile to observable traces.

7
00:00:38,844 --> 00:00:41,129
Both repositories are linked here.

8
00:00:42,029 --> 00:00:48,406
Judges do not need to author JSON or understand Logons before trying the product.

9
00:00:48,406 --> 00:00:56,606
Seven built-in packets cover grounded answers, branching evidence, parallel tools, self-correction, multi-agent handoffs, conflicting sources, and program-scale work.

10
00:00:56,606 --> 00:01:03,439
Each is a deterministic teaching fixture that runs through the real validation and scoring path.

11
00:01:04,339 --> 00:01:11,180
Each Logon is one observable atomic unit: a request, tool result, check, contradiction, or output.

12
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:16,652
Typed edges show how those units support, constrain, or challenge one another.

13
00:01:16,652 --> 00:01:26,685
SOL Lens replays the packet locally, scores evidence, coherence, and unresolved contradiction, then applies explicit gates to return PROMOTE, HOLD, or QUARANTINE.

14
00:01:27,585 --> 00:01:31,692
The conflicting-sources packet compares six evidence branches across one hundred twenty Logons.

15
00:01:31,692 --> 00:01:39,907
Contradiction rises from point zero nine in the reference trace to point two four in the candidate, moving the court from PROMOTE to QUARANTINE.

16
00:01:39,907 --> 00:01:45,384
A candidate can look productive while its observable evidence structure shows that it is not ready.

17
00:01:46,284 --> 00:01:54,224
Every verdict can be exported as a versioned proof packet containing the observable Logons, typed edges, metrics, and recomputed court result.

18
00:01:54,224 --> 00:01:59,895
There are no hidden-chain-of-thought claims, and the same packet can be independently validated and replayed.

19
00:02:00,795 --> 00:02:07,548
The optional Manifold Replay asks a different question: how might semantic activity propagate through this observable graph?

20
00:02:08,448 --> 00:02:15,285
Each deterministic step updates dynamic density and pressure, computes mode-shaped conductance and edge flux, and applies damping.

21
00:02:15,285 --> 00:02:20,915
The telemetry makes graph dynamics inspectable without inventing missing events or exposing hidden reasoning.

22
00:02:20,915 --> 00:02:29,360
It is an experimental visualization layer: replay state stays separate from the packet and never changes the authoritative Trace Court verdict.

23
00:02:30,260 --> 00:02:39,547
SOL Lens was built during OpenAI Build Week with GPT-5.6 and Codex on top of the pre-existing SOL research program.

24
00:02:39,547 --> 00:02:45,120
The linked repositories provide the mathematics, experiments, tests, provenance, and application source.

25
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:52,085
SOL Lens makes agent migration evidence visible, deterministic, and reviewable before a workflow reaches production.

